From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daigorian <apps@daigorian.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mb86h61: re-cut the SPI-NOR partitions for the OpenIRD layout

The vendor layout gives the root filesystem 1MB and spends 12MB on two
6MB application slots (slot0/slot1) that only the vendor userland uses.
OpenIRD does not need them, so the 13MB from 0x2C0000 to 0xFC0000 is
re-cut as a 5MB read-only rootfs, a 7MB writable overlay (the upper
layer of overlayfs) and a 1MB recovery rootfs.

The first six partitions are left alone: libooter reads the boot loader,
its environment, the slot info and the kernel slot directly, and the
kernel image itself must stay at 0x140000.

Two constraints shaped the layout:

 - rootfs keeps its 0x2C0000 start.  Installing this kernel is a
   separate step from installing a new root filesystem, so the root
   filesystem that is already in flash has to keep working with the new
   partition table.

 - "slot info1" is preserved.  It is a byte-for-byte copy of "slot
   info0" (both hold the same 44-byte "TOLS" record), and it is not
   known whether libooter falls back to it, so it is not worth the
   64KB to find out.  "reserved" (192KB, erased) is kept for the same
   reason.

The recovery partition holds a small root filesystem that carries the
mtd utility.  A squashfs root cannot rewrite the partition it is running
from, and once the vendor slots are gone there is no other writer left
in flash, so without it recovering from a bad image would need a SPI-NOR
clip.

Signed-off-by: Daigorian <apps@daigorian.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-mb86hxx/mb86h61_devkit.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/mach-mb86hxx/mb86h61_devkit.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-mb86hxx/mb86h61_devkit.c
@@ -448,29 +448,33 @@
 		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64) * SIZE_1PAGE,
 		.size = 1536 * SIZE_1PAGE,
 	},
+	/* OpenIRD: mtd6 以降を切り直す。mtd0-5 (libooter/env/slot info0/nvram/kernel)
+	 * は libooter が見るので不変。rootfs は 0x2C0000 開始を保つ（区画表だけを
+	 * 差し替えた新カーネルで、既存の rootfs がそのまま起動できるようにするため）。
+	 * slot info1 は slot info0 と同内容の冗長面なので温存する。 */
 	{
-		.name = "rootfs",
-		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 1536) * SIZE_1PAGE,
-		.size = 1024 * SIZE_1PAGE,
+		.name = "rootfs",			/* squashfs (RO) */
+		.offset = 2816 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 0x2C0000 */
+		.size = 5120 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 5MB */
 	},
 	{
-		.name = "slot0",
-		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 1536 + 1024) * SIZE_1PAGE,
-		.size = 6 * 1024 * SIZE_1PAGE,
+		.name = "rootfs_data",			/* overlayfs upper (jffs2) */
+		.offset = 7936 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 0x7C0000 */
+		.size = 7168 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 7MB */
 	},
 	{
-		.name = "slot1",
-		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 1536 + 1024 + 6*1024) * SIZE_1PAGE,
-		.size = 6 * 1024 * SIZE_1PAGE,
+		.name = "firstaid",			/* 復旧用 rootfs (squashfs, RO) */
+		.offset = 15104 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 0xEC0000 */
+		.size = 1024 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 1MB */
 	},
 	{
 		.name = "slot info1",
-		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 1536 + 1024 + 6*1024 + 6*1024) * SIZE_1PAGE,
+		.offset = 16128 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 0xFC0000 */
 		.size = 64 * SIZE_1PAGE
 	},
 	{
 		.name = "reserved",
-		.offset = (1024 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 64 + 1536 + 1024 + 6*1024 + 6*1024 + 64) * SIZE_1PAGE,
+		.offset = 16192 * SIZE_1PAGE,		/* 0xFD0000 */
 		.size = 192 * SIZE_1PAGE
 	}
 };
